     "page": 1,
     "text": "Hanson Fisher and Solis Medical Group\nRe: Kevin Wilson (DOB 03/31/1946)\n\nJanuary 23, 2026: Mr. Kevin Wilson visited today for a medication refill. His blood pressure was measured at 140/81, and his weight was 206 pounds. Mr. Wilson reports feeling well overall. His blood pressure has been stable, and he is adhering to his medication regimen without any issues. He has been diligent monitoring his blood sugar levels and maintaining a healthy lifestyle. \n\nJuly 17, 2025: Mr. Wilson came in today for a routine medication refill. His blood pressure was recorded at 149/81, and his weight was 209 pounds. He continues to manage his Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose, with an A1c of 6.1. He also has glaucoma, which is well-controlled. Mr. Wilson reports no significant changes in his vision or any other concerning symptoms.\n\nJanuary 07, 2025: Mr. Wilson visited due to acute His blood pressure was 135/83, and his weight was 196 pounds. He is doing well post-treatment and has recovered from the sinusitis episode. His other conditions, including Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose and glaucoma, remain stable. \n\nJune 30, 2024: Mr. Wilson came in today for a routine visit related to a URI. His blood pressure was 135/86, and his weight was 196 pounds. He is feeling better now, and his symptoms have resolved. His other chronic conditions, Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose and glaucoma, are well-managed. His A1c remains at 6.2, which is within the target range.\n\nDecember 22, 2023: Mr. Wilson visited today regarding erectile dysfunction. His blood pressure was 144/86, and his weight was 198 pounds. He is doing well in managing his erectile dysfunction with medications such as tadalafil 20 and sildenafil 100 mg. His Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose is well-controlled with an A1c of 6.1, and his glaucoma is stable. \n\nAdditionally, Mr. Wilson has a family history of significant medical conditions. His father passed away at the age of 54 from colon canc